      "question": "Simplify: ∛(54)",
      "choices": {
        "A": "3∛2",
        "B": "3∛5",
        "C": "2∛3",
        "D": "5∛3",
        "E": "∛54 (cannot simplify)"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "explanation": "54 = 27 × 2 = 3³ × 2. So ∛54 = ∛(3³ × 2) = 3∛2.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Factor 54: 54 = 27 × 2 = 3³ × 2.",
        "2. Apply radical: ∛(3³ × 2) = ∛(3³) × ∛2.",
        "3. Simplify: 3 × ∛2 = 3∛2."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Extract perfect cubes from cube root."
